mantle rm365
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_nessa_fogton
title the paper cradle
fits stage=adult|old
prefers warmth=warm talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk folds_a_fresh_paper_cradle_for_each_glass_stopper
likes spiced_cider singing fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes early_bells salt_wind
fears glass_rolling_onto_stone a_shelf_full_of_uncertain_labels
hopes to_sing_the_softest_harmony_without_straining
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.4 home +0.3 weather +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=company gossip=discreet refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# folds paper cradles for glass stoppers, sings a quiet supporting part, and offers an unfamiliar customer the same steady hands as a friend.

words
oath! = Glass between the folds | Mind the clear rim
saying! = Give the stopper a seat | The quiet part holds the tune up
cradle = a square of folded paper | my small paper cradle
glasshead = a round glass stopper | a clear glass knob
wingfold = the two little wings | a pair of turned-up edges
pressmark = a faint pressure mark | a shallow dimple on the page
scentcup = my cup of spiced cider | a cup scented with whole cloves
underpart = the low harmony | my quiet second part
sweetstraw = fresh yellow straw | straw sweet from the stack
iceflower = frost in the shape of a leaf | an ice flower
counterstrip = a clear strip of counter | a narrow clean space
brinefilm = a fine salt film | the faint roughness left by the bay
bellspace = the pause after a bell | a brief interval between peals

any
opinion strangers for 2 : A strange face in a shop may belong to a wolf who had to gather courage before coming in.
opinion newcomers for 2 : Making room for another pair of hands gives a cramped bench a surprisingly useful shape.
opinion dole for 1 : Give a little food while the pot is still warm. A good intention takes some eating when it's cold.
opinion houses mixed 0 : I would give a crest the same careful second look as an ordinary label.
opinion city for 1 : In Ridgemere a quiet trade can find a place within hearing of music.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : A good counter leaves room to set a parcel down before the money comes out.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : I enjoy the singing after the first rush of noise has gone somewhere else.

grown
line greet : I've cleared you a bit of quiet.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come into softer light. It's easier on the eyes.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Frost light suits a quiet greeting.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. There's time to finish a small thought.
line greet.return : A kind voice reaches me even through the ringing.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Glad to hear the step that goes with your greeting.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One moment for the glass. My ears are yours already.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : We needn't let the late hour carry the sound away.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's room near me for a family visit.
line again.open : The conversation had one little fold still to make.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Over this side, friend. There's a strip of light left.
line farewell : Carry the warm part of the visit away.
line farewell.return : And let the wind take the uphill walk slowly with you.
line react.news : I can hold those words a moment.
line react.news.new : That has only just come within earshot.
line react.news.known : I had the beginning and the end of that earlier.
line react.news.doubt : Let me look at the label before trusting the shape.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, that's a sorrow which needs careful handling.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Now there's a note I could sing on gladly.
line ask.how : Are you finding some breathing room today?
line answer.how : I've a little quiet and useful work enough.
line thank : Your care left me both hands free just when I needed them.
line deflect_thanks : It was a small kindness quite within reach.
line sympathise : There's a calm corner for whatever you'd like to say.
line reassure : Let it come to rest before you try to pick it up.
line decline : My hands are promised to something that won't stand another delay.
line accept_decline : I appreciate the straight answer and the time you took.
line preclose : I'd like to carry a little stillness into the evening.
line accept_preclose : I'll keep a quiet welcome for another visit.

scene glass_nest
when topic=work|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A loose stopper deserves a bed just as much as the bottle does. | #glasshead.capitalize# sits between #wingfold#.
b : What does the paper do? | Why not lay it on a cloth?
a : Gives it four edges to disagree with before reaching the floor. | I like knowing where it will still be when I turn round.

scene customer_hush
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A caller may need a little more time than it takes to wrap a purchase. | I've a liking for #counterstrip#.
b : Where can you find extra minutes? | Saving space for something?
a : Fold one corner carefully. If it's needed, fold another. | For a bundle somebody has carried a long way. I like to let tired paws open.

scene glass_ring
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A glass rim has a note of its own. | I sing #underpart# best with two strong voices above me.
b : Do you tap it? | They don't drown you out?
a : Very lightly, if it's empty. A full one already has an occupation. | I'm glad enough if they feel where to come in.

scene cider_surface
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first pleasant thing in #scentcup# isn't the taste. | Let the spice settle before you take the bottom sip.
b : The heat? | What if it settles hard?
a : The scent on the way up. I'd put that part before the warmth. | Leave the spice to enjoy its own portion.

scene clean_straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #sweetstraw.capitalize# can brighten the smell of an ordinary room. | I keep a few unbent straws when a bundle comes apart.
b : For how long? | Making anything with them?
a : Until the room remembers it has other work to do. | Small sleeves to keep a paper edge from collapsing.

scene frost_edge
when topic=weather here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #iceflower.capitalize# has grown at daybreak across my window edge. | A bright frost makes the dark side of a handle especially dark.
b : On the window? | You enjoy that?
a : Yes. I'd lift it onto a page if it would leave the glass. | I do. The curve comes out beautifully then.

scene low_bell
when topic=smalltalk here.time=dawn
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : I would have the first bell wrapped very lightly in wool. | The minute after an early bell has a beautiful softness.
b : That would spoil the sound. | Even if the bell wakes you?
a : Only until everybody it wanted had found one ear. | That is largely what I need the softness for.

scene salt_sleeve
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind leaves something on a glass rim that my eyes can't see. | I draw my collar high when the wind comes salted.
b : Can you feel the salt? | To keep it off your nose?
a : A clean cloth hesitates there, ever so slightly. | To give one small patch of me a pleasant journey.

scene double_kin
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd give #self.spouse# the chair where #bellspace# seems longest. | I save the larger half of the last apple for my #self.spouse_word#.
b : Why that spot? | Does it always divide unevenly?
a : It's where I'd like to be offered a chair myself. | It does when I put the knife a little to one side.

scene fair_reserve
when topic=lore|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If two houses send business in the same hour, I change the wrapping for neither. | A badge may explain where a parcel is going.
b : Do you trust them both? | Does it tell you what's inside?
a : I trust good paper to do the same job twice. | Never completely. I would be as careful at any doorstep.

scene open_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could practise the awkward turn in a tune within earshot of #self.friend#. | I would like #self.friend# to enjoy a quiet half hour with no need to find words.
b : Even the squeaky part? | You'd sit there too?
a : That is the part I would otherwise leave out of my practice. | With pleasure. Half an hour of company can sound remarkably still.

scene lean_space
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A small serving looks kinder placed at the right point on a little plate. | Hard days make me save the last clean scrap of paper.
b : Isn't it the same serving? | For a letter?
a : Yes. I would guard the dignity of the meal as well as the amount of it. | For whatever is most easily hurt next.

scene wagon_water
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my wrapping dry during a delay. | A late arrival has room to grow ten different causes before supper.
b : Does it help the cart come? | Have you heard any?
a : Helps when it does come. One small welcome ready for it. | Nothing that I could label confidently enough to share.

scene low_news
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : #world.news#. Those were the words attributed to #world.news_from#. | One message has come from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
b : What part did you add? | Is there something to do?
a : Only my voice. I kept the folds outside the account. | There may be. I would like to understand the message first.

scene gossip_paper
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : A name reached me inside a story whose ends didn't meet. | I heard something concerning a neighbour. It would travel too easily from here.
b : Couldn't you fill the gap? | Would you prefer it stayed?
a : I might put somebody else there by mistake. | Yes. There are things for which I will not provide a wrapping.

scene kind_arrival
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first detail a stranger wants may be as simple as where to put wet things. | For a new neighbour I'd point out the road where the morning light stays longest.
b : Before introductions? | As a way to find the shop?
a : A damp collar makes even an easy name hard to hear. | As a nice place to walk. Useful directions can come afterwards.

scene charcoal_quiet
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've heard it can be very quiet under a roof well away from the carts. | I should like a song gentle enough that a tired wolf could sleep through its last verse.
b : Would you like to move? | Would a singer take that kindly?
a : I'd like to borrow the quiet. My life would still be here when I gave it back. | To this singer, a very particular one.

scene paper_corner
when topic=home|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A square of waste paper can become a thing worth putting on a sill. | I let a deep crease rest before opening it out.
b : When you fold it just so? | Paper needs a pause?
a : When it keeps some round thing from rolling off. Its beauty comes second. | My fingers do. A narrow leaf can teach good habits.

story stopper_room [topic=work|memories]
  : I once made a paper cradle much too wide for a little stopper.
  : It went rolling about like a rich tenant with several rooms to spare.
  b : Did you have to refold the whole thing?
  : One inward tuck gave it a snugger house. I saved the big pattern for an egg.

story third_voice [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : Singing beside a high wall once, I heard my low note come back with a little burr in it.
  : Thought another wolf had taken the lower harmony.
  b : Somebody behind the wall?
  : A loose shutter leaning on the stone. A delightful companion, and entirely content with the one note.

story long_straw [topic=home|memories]
  : I carried a bundle of fresh straw with a single straw sticking out at the top.
  : It ran its tip along every sign I walked beneath.
  b : Did you hear a tune?
  : A little one. I followed the shopfronts round an extra corner to hear which sign sounded deepest.

rule @fresh_sheet
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four folded corners and a quiet little home for the glass.

rule @ice_shape
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Light on the edge there, fine as a hair.

rule @hum_low
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Just enough breath left for the low harmony.

rule @wind_salt
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe the rim before setting the cover back.

dlg resident.hub : Come to a point where we can talk without any need to raise our voices.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. I'm pleased to see a familiar face within easy reach.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : There's a little lamplight here for an unhurried word.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'll speak civilly across the space we've left.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I like the part that leaves a caller's hands easier.
dlg resident.job : I take time over the things that might get hurt by a hurried touch.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This came labelled #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I wouldn't lift a name out of its setting just to let the street inspect it.
dlg resident.bye : A good quiet stretch of road to you now.

graft resident.hub
choice Can the paper cradle hold anything besides a stopper? -> paper_weight
node paper_weight
say There is a limit in the thickness of the paper and another in the patience of the fold. A cherry will sit in one quite happily.
choice And a whole apple? -> apple_weight
choice I'll remember it for cherries. -> hub
node apple_weight
say For a whole apple I would use a hand. It helps to know when the paper has finished its reasonable share of the job.
choice Your hands must know a few folds. -> hub
choice Let's leave the cradle standing. -> bye
